EBS Volume vs EBS Snapshot

EBS Volume:
- Stored at the Availability Zone (AZ) level.
- Can be attached only to an EC2 instance in the same AZ.
- Cannot be directly attached to an EC2 instance in another AZ.

EBS Snapshot:
- Stored at the Region level.
- Not tied to any specific AZ.
- Can be used to create new EBS volumes in any AZ within the same Region.
- To use a snapshot in another Region, it must first be copied to that Region.

Interview One-Liner:

EBS Volumes are AZ-specific, whereas EBS Snapshots are Region-specific.
